WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.072
Use these questions as a quick check before finishing the module.

00:00:04.072 --> 00:00:06.862
Can you explain what a variable is?

00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:12.342
Can you tell the difference between an integer, float, string, and Boolean?

00:00:12.342 --> 00:00:17.125
Can you trace a calculation from input values to a final result?

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:20.679
Also think about formatting and conversion.

00:00:20.679 --> 00:00:24.264
Why would we display a decimal as a percentage?

00:00:24.264 --> 00:00:30.419
Why might the text “29.99” need conversion before arithmetic?

00:00:30.419 --> 00:00:33.814
You do not need to memorize every symbol yet.

00:00:33.814 --> 00:00:39.468
What matters is understanding the concepts well enough to recognize what Python needs.
